    [31m[39m
    [31m    // The dot field is deliberately inert — no cursor-proximity shimmer.[39m
    [31m    // The map is the backdrop; only the pins and cards respond to hover.[39m
    [31m[39m
    [31m    // ── The scroll frame ──[39m
    [31m    // One passive listener, one rAF, idle whenever the section is off[39m
    [31m    // screen. Drives both the dot scrub and the card swell.[39m
    [31m    //[39m
    [31m    // ── Card swell on approach ──[39m
    [31m    // Each card scales up as its OWN centre climbs toward the viewport[39m
    [31m    // midline, then eases back down over a longer distance — so HQ swells[39m
    [31m    // and settles, then Latin America does, and the two overlap into one[39m
    [31m    // continuous motion instead of two synchronized blips.[39m
    [31m    //[39m
    [31m    // The scale lives on .mapx-slot, not .mapx-card, for two reasons:[39m
    [31m    // the card owns the 1.07 hover scale (same property — one would[39m
    [31m    // clobber the other), and the connector arcs are cached to the slot's[39m
    [31m    // centre, which a centre-origin scale never moves. So arcs stay[39m
    [31m    // anchored with no per-frame geometry rebuild.[39m
    [31m    {[39m
    [31m      const PEAK = 0.04;       // +4% at the midline — stays under hover's 1.07[39m
    [31m      const RISE = 0.5;        // viewport heights of run-up (quick)[39m
    [31m      const FALL = 0.95;       // ...and of fall-off (slow)[39m
    [31m      const NARROW = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 880px)');  // cards go full-width[39m
    [31m      let geo = [], raf = 0, live = false;[39m
    [31m[39m
    [31m      function measure() {[39m
